      ":question/problem": "![](images/bc/bc8d8e89d8d9a40322b4efd3a5c04b03648762fc5d4985bbf764abdc4c93c89f.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $AC^(\u27f7)\u2225A_{1}C_{1}^(\u27f7)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The sum of the measures of the interior angles of $\u25b3ABC$ equals $180^{\u2218}$.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $AC^(\u27f7)\u2225A_{1}C_{1}^(\u27f7)$ | Given |\n| 2 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $m\u2220ABC_{1} = m\u2220BAC$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 4 | $\u2220A_{1}BC\u2245\u2220BCA$ | Alternate interior angles theorem |\n| 5 | $m\u2220A_{1}BC = m\u2220BCA$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 6 | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n| 7 | $m\u2220ABC_{1} + m\u2220ABC + m\u2220A_{1}BC$<br>$= m\u2220A_{1}BC_{1}$ | Angle addition postulate |\n| 8 | $m\u2220BAC + m\u2220ABC + m\u2220BCA$<br>$= m\u2220A_{1}BC_{1}$ | Substitution |\n| 9 | $m\u2220BAC + m\u2220ABC + m\u2220BCA$<br>$= 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-5}} |"
    },
